SparkOS is published so people can read how it is made. It is not open source.

What you may do:

1. Read the source code and documentation in this repository.
2. Download the official SparkOS installer and system images that Wolklaw publishes
   (the releases of github.com/Wolklaw/sparkos and the images at ghcr.io/wolklaw/sparkos),
   install them on your own computers and use them, including their automatic updates.
3. Fork this repository on GitHub and change, build and test your fork on your own computers,
   to propose those changes back to this repository as a pull request. This does not let you
   publish or distribute images, installers or builds made from a fork.

What you may not do without written permission from Wolklaw, except as item 3 above allows:

1. Copy, modify, translate or adapt the code, artwork, sounds or documentation in this
   repository, or make works based on them.
2. Build, publish or distribute your own SparkOS images, installers or modified versions.
3. Redistribute, sell, rent or sublicense SparkOS or any part of this repository, or use
   any part of it in another product or service.
4. Use the SparkOS name, logo or bot artwork for anything that is not the official SparkOS.

GitHub's Terms of Service let GitHub users view and fork public repositories on GitHub. A
fork made under those terms gives no other right than item 3 above; everything above still
applies to it.

Contributions. When you send a contribution to SparkOS (a pull request, a patch, or code, text
or artwork in an issue), you confirm that you made it or have the right to send it, and you give
Wolklaw a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, perpetual and irrevocable license to use, copy,
modify, publish, distribute and sublicense it, as part of SparkOS or otherwise, under any terms,
including this license. You keep your copyright. Wolklaw doesn't have to merge or use anything.
If a contribution contains work made by others, say so in the pull request and give its license;
it is then listed in THIRD-PARTY.md.

Parts made by others keep their own licenses and are not covered by this license. They are
listed in THIRD-PARTY.md. The SparkOS image also contains Fedora, Bazzite, KDE and other
software under their own licenses; this license does not limit your rights under those.

